NNAAMMEE
     eellffccttll — change an ELF binary's feature control note

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     eellffccttll [--hh | ----hheellpp] [--ii] [--ll] [--ee _f_e_a_t_u_r_e_l_i_s_t] _f_i_l_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The eellffccttll utility modifies feature flags in the feature control note in
     an ELF binary.

     The options are as follows:

     --hh | ----hheellpp
             Print a usage message and exit.

     --ii      Ignore unknown feature flags in _f_e_a_t_u_r_e_l_i_s_t.

     --ll      List known ELF feature flags.

     --ee _f_e_a_t_u_r_e_l_i_s_t
             Edit features from the given comma separated list _f_e_a_t_u_r_e_l_i_s_t.
             _f_e_a_t_u_r_e_l_i_s_t starts with one of the three operations: “+” to turn
             on the features, “-” to turn off the features, “=” to only turn
             on the given features.  A comma separated list of feature names
             or numeric values follows the operation.

     If --ee is not specified eellffccttll displays the status of each feature in the
     ELF note in each _f_i_l_e _._._..

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     Exit status is 0 on success, and 1 if the command fails if a file does
     not exist, is too short, or fails to find or edit features note.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     The following is an example of a typical usage of the eellffccttll command:

           elfctl file
           elfctl -e +noaslr file

     Features may be specified as numerical values:

           elfctl -e =0x0001,0x0004 file

     Features may also be specified as a single combined value:

           elfctl -e =0x5 file

